Score the prompt below from 0 to {escala_max} on each rubric criterion.

RUBRIC:
{criterios}

Return ONLY this JSON object, no markdown, no preamble:
{"puntajes": {"{claves}"}, "diagnostico": "one short sentence per criterion scored below {umbral}", "secciones": {"sujeto": "...", "composicion": "...", "luz": "...", "estilo": "...", "camara": "..."}}

`secciones` is the REWRITE: return it only when some criterion scores below {umbral} (otherwise return an empty object). Keep every section in English, 15-26 words, prose, and fix ONLY what the low scores point at — do not restyle what already works. Never write the text-to-render, the typography, the format line or the negatives: the app owns those four sections and will re-attach them verbatim. The app also prefixes a WORLD LOCK to `sujeto`, prefixes a LIGHT LOCK to `luz` and appends the lockup, the beat shot and the SET ARC to `composicion` — those clauses are re-attached too, so never restate them, never relocate the set, never change which object the arc says this piece shows, and never write a shot distance into `sujeto`.
